test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T07:50:51.9253569Z             "body": "Preserves original Playwright MCP tools and adds a bounded local batch/jobs companion. Publishing stays disabled. **Draft; not release-ready.**\n\nLatest completed native79 at `d357c385203c342a3f39a927ff06eba9eabded59`: **1,905 reported test passes / 8 failures**, plus Mac actual-Codex TIMED_OUT973 and two failed Windows JSON controls. [Batch QA](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39735545547):1,446/6; [original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39735545519):459/2. Both workflows fail. All17 non-soak jobs conclude; optional soak skips; reported test skips/cancellations0.\n\nOwnership failures remain explicit: Windows guardian disconnect returns136 legacy candidates; Windows WebKit privacy verifies all8 HTTP scenarios then returns142 audit candidates. Neither fixture captured the necessary live browser/model birth ledgers. Every candidate remains unclassified; overlap is unknown. Audit-helper role and before-window counts exclude nothing and clear no debt.\n\nOther failures: Windows all-action Firefox9/23 check-pointer timeout (14/15 cases pass overall), Mac SDK971 lifecycle timeout, Windows raw pipe fifth12/23 locator timeout and Firefox429 lifecycle timeout after navigation acknowledgement, and two original Windows Firefox screenshot/popup timeouts. Later cases within failed flows and Windows legacy follow-up remain unexecuted. Original Linux/Mac152 each, Docker2 and Mac modal3 pass. Linux/Windows actual-Codex1k pass with model0/owned0; Mac973 fails with known terminated/removed cleanup. Private-temp9/10 close failure and inherited9/10 locator failure remain failed despite zero observed residuals. Healthy later controls do not explain earlier failures.\n\nFive175-file installs,15 cancellation cases (60 scenarios), five strict ownership units and five supervised/raw20-screenshot fixtures pass. No new actual-root failure receipt occurs naturally in native79; local real-Firefox negative imports the unchanged test, invokes actual close/kill then withholds return ACKs: expected exit1,23 actions,two cleanup failures,exitObserved:true. Root exit never proves tree cleanup.\n\nLocal follow-up only: HTTP privacy reuses the existing actual factory gate, capturing supervisor/worker/browser births before HTTP effects and retaining complete same-snapshot legacy rows/root rows. Guardian disconnect records the actual fork and model-child lifetime before disconnect, retains full comparisons and preserves failed workspaces. Canonical outcomes, all eight HTTP/privacy checks, zero-owned assertions and all budgets remain. No generic process-matching, termination, lease, dependency, schema, browser/channel or transport changes. Final local guardian/graph/cleanup24/24 eachNode22/24; real HTTP2/2 eachNode20/22/24 (16 scenarios each lane), Linux Chromium/Firefox only; WebKit unexecuted. Intermediate phases are saved separately. Fresh175-file production install, syntax/lint/diff checks pass. Native80 is running at `bea4780d370deec0c36ae64c965dfc24157b385d`: [Batch QA](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39739439069), [original CI](https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39739439372). Pending is not PASS; no causal fix or retrospective classification is claimed.\n\nAll17 job logs and EOF retry receipt saved under docs/evidence/worker-ci-seventyninth-* and native79-*. No artifact download/auth/TLS workaround, deadline raises, forced/replayed input or PID-based debt clearance. G00–G18 remain incomplete; execution ledger/report preserve unsupported scope and historical uncertainty. No merge or release requested.\n",
